<title>DENMARK: Neurosearch offers 160,830 new shares.</title>
<headline>Neurosearch offers 160,830 new shares.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish biotech company Neurosearch said on Friday that it would issue 160,830 new 20-crown shares to shareholders wishing to exercise their warrants.</p>
<p>A Neurosearch statement said that after the issue the firm's share capital would be over 117.124 million crowns nominal value, corresponding to 5,124,420 shares.</p>
<p>The share price closed on Friday -- before the announcement -- at 410 crowns, up 26 from Thursday's close. --Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
